{{also|жэ}}
==Old Church Slavonic==

===Etymology ===
From {{inh|cu|sla-pro|*že}}, from {{inh|cu|ine-bsl-pro|*ge}}, from {{inh|cu|ine-pro|*gʰe|*ǵʰi}}.

===Conjunction===
{{head|cu|conjunction}}

# [[and]]
#* from the ''Vita Constantini'':
#*: {{quote|cu|егда '''же''' и роди мати...|'''And''' when his mother bore him...}}
#* from the ''Vita Methodii'':
#*: {{quote|cu|по сихъ '''же''' вьсѣхъ ...|'''And''' after all these ...}}
# [[but]]
# [[however]]
#* from the ''Vita Constantini'':
#*: {{quote|cu|отроче '''же''' не рачи се ѥти тꙋждь съсьць никакоже, развѣ по матерꙿнꙇи, донꙿдеже ѡтьдоѥнь бꙑсть.|'''However''', until the child was weaned he would not take any other breast but his mother’s.}}
# [[then]]
#* from the ''Vita Constantini'':
#*: {{quote|cu|онь '''же''' рече: вѣрꙋ ми ими, жено|'''Then''' he said: “Believe me, wife, I place my hope in God.}}
# [[after]]
#* from the ''Vita Methodii'':
#*: {{quote|cu|сътворь '''же''' въ томь кнѧжии лѣта многа |'''After''' spending many years in that principality}}
# [[as]]
#* from the ''Homily against the Bogumils'', 329:
#*: {{quote|cu|о крьстѣ '''же''' господьни ...|'''As''' for the Lord's cross ...}}

===References===
* ''Old Church Slavonic: An Elementary Grammar'' by S. C. Gardiner, Cambridge University Press, 2008.

